WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.557
Hi, I'm Jetty!

00:00:02.557 --> 00:00:05.663
Skyfall's new model turns one picture of a machine into a

00:00:05.663 --> 00:00:06.792
plan for building it.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:12.326
A language model writes one long program.

00:00:12.326 --> 00:00:16.070
This model splits the machine into a tree of parts, then draws

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.941
each part's build, many at once.

00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:22.112
It starts from a single image of the product.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:26.493
The composer decides what it is made of, one level at a time.

00:00:26.913 --> 00:00:29.491
The construction model works out how each leaf is built.

00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:33.104
Together: a tree, and a build sequence for every part.

00:00:34.817 --> 00:00:36.358
The composer has three steps.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.835
First, a rough shape of the whole object.

00:00:39.337 --> 00:00:42.705
Then it splits it into assemblies, and those again, side by side.

00:00:43.125 --> 00:00:45.862
Then a refiner fills in what the rough shape never had.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:50.382
For one part, it first plans the solid after every step.

00:00:50.802 --> 00:00:53.695
Between each pair of states, it draws the sketch that turns

00:00:53.695 --> 00:00:54.747
one into the next.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:58.172
Each drawing is rolled out roughly first, in a compressed space.

00:00:58.592 --> 00:01:01.567
Then a refiner adds sharp lines and exact corners.

00:01:03.342 --> 00:01:04.433
Here is one sketch.

00:01:04.433 --> 00:01:06.068
On the left, the target outline.

00:01:06.488 --> 00:01:10.392
In the middle, the latent rollout: the layout is right, the corners are soft.

00:01:10.812 --> 00:01:14.032
On the right, the refined rollout, redrawn at full resolution.

00:01:15.425 --> 00:01:19.972
On Skyfall's CAD benchmark, it matches GPT-6 Astra on accuracy, and reports

00:01:19.972 --> 00:01:24.898
doing it fifty-one times faster, at a hundred and fiftieth of the cost.

00:01:26.183 --> 00:01:27.680
The tree shortens the wait.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.177
Small latents cut the cost.

00:01:29.177 --> 00:01:32.770
But today the output is a visual plan, and an editable CAD

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:34.566
file is still on the roadmap.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.392
Split it into a tree.

00:01:37.392 --> 00:01:39.182
Plan the states, then the sketches.

00:01:39.182 --> 00:01:40.376
Rough first, detail last.

00:01:40.796 --> 00:01:42.844
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:42.844 --> 00:01:43.429
I'm Jetty.

00:01:43.429 --> 00:01:43.722
Bye!
